\begin{remark}[Conjecture: general two-dimensional CFTs]\label{rem:twobranch-general}
For $\cA=\cA_{\rm chiral}\otimes\overline{\cA}_{\rm chiral}$ with general chiral halves of central charges $c,\bar c$ we conjecture \eqref{eq:twobranch}, with $\Phi_c$ the single-chirality zero-collar recovery error of the chiral half.  The argument above would need (i) the factorisation of the rotated Petz map into chiral rotated maps with parameters $t$ and $-t$, and (ii) a per-chirality function $\Phi_c$: the collapse of \cref{cor:collapse} and the normal extension behind it are proved only for the free fermion, and for a general chiral net only the second-order coefficient $f_2=c/(12\pi^2)$ is known.
\end{remark}
